# Agent UI selectors

**Full decision tree, budgets, and verify close-out:** read [`.cursor/skills/agent-ui/SKILL.md`](../skills/agent-ui/SKILL.md) before simulator work.

## Always add an ID

When you create or edit an interactive / agent-tappable control, same change:

1. Constant in [`src/utils/agent-ui/ids.ts`](../../src/utils/agent-ui/ids.ts) → `ontrack.<feature>.<surface>.<control>`
2. `testID` / `useAgentUiTarget` / `AgentTestId`
3. Document in [`docs/agent-ui-map.md`](../../docs/agent-ui-map.md)

Layout anchors (major sections): `AgentTestId` without `onPress` → `ontrack.<feature>.<surface>.section.<name>`.

Coordinates are not an alternative. Screenshot bugs → [`screenshot-triage.mdc`](./screenshot-triage.mdc).

## Navigation (stop at first match)

0. Stuck → [`stuck-check-config.mdc`](./stuck-check-config.mdc)
1. App up via `once`/`verify`/`flow` (or `ensure-packager.sh --start`)
2. Already on route → `./scripts/agent-ui.sh verify --route …`
3. Else `once --flow` / `agent-ui-flow.sh` / `agent-ui-open.sh` / known `agent-ui-tap.sh`
4. Unknown id → **one** dump; else add testID
5. Assert / `--color` then **STOP** (see [`show-simulator-screenshot.mdc`](./show-simulator-screenshot.mdc))

JS key paths work (`travel.planDetail.transportSection`). Off-screen: `agent-ui-scroll` — never host CGEvent swipes.

## Do not

Dump “just to be sure”; re-run `once --flow` when `verify --route` fits; mid-flow / ritual handoff screenshots; tab-hop; prophylactic `ensure-packager`; ship interactive UI without `ontrack.*` ids.
